---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';

const title = 'Work';
const description =
  'Products and projects by Priya Kaur, including markAtt, an attendance and homework tracking app built for a community Sunday school in Brisbane.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Work</h1>

  <p class="lead">This is where the products and projects I build live.</p>

  <div class="divide">
    <article class="entry">
      <div class="entry__head">
        <h2>markAtt</h2>
        <Status state="in-pilot" />
      </div>

      <p>
        markAtt is an attendance and homework tracking app for a community
        Sunday school in Brisbane. Teachers open it at the start of a session,
        mark who is present, and record whether homework was completed.
      </p>

      <p>
        It replaced a Google Sheets workflow — shared tabs per class, edited on
        phones, with no reliable way to tell who had changed what. The app gives
        each teacher only their own class, and keeps one mark per student per
        session against the date it was taken.
      </p>

      <p>
        It is built with React Native and Expo on the front end, and Supabase
        for the database and authentication. Access is enforced with row-level
        security rather than in the client, so a teacher cannot read another
        class's records even if the app is wrong.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/markatt/support/">markAtt support and contact</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <!--
    Later: the full markAtt case study goes here, after the pilot term.
    Cover the Google Sheets workflow it replaced, the data model, the
    row-level security policies, and what the pilot actually surfaced.
  -->
</Base>
